--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
IMPLEMENTATION NOTES (SwiftUI / HIG)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
• Catalog built from `AppRoute.allCases` grouped by `AppRouteGroup` — the native single-source-of-truth,
  exactly as the web page re-uses the sidebar `navSections`. Search corpus = humanized identifier +
  group + canonical path; filter is case-insensitive AND-token (web filterFeatureCatalog parity).
• Design tokens only (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius); shared components only
  (TSGlassPanel, TSCard, TSButton, TSIconBox, TSPageTitle, TSErrorDisplay, ContentUnavailableView,
  TSSkeleton…); native material via TSGlassPanel (ADR-005). No web cloning, no raw library imports.
• Adaptive (ADR-002/006): FeatureCard grid uses `GridItem(.adaptive(minimum:240))` so it reflows
  macOS/iPad regular ↔ iPhone compact. Sticky search uses a pinned LazyVStack section header.
• a11y (ADR-015): combined elements + labels/traits on cards, chips, search field, anchor strip;
  Dynamic Type via system fonts + .teslaSyncTheme(); light/dark via the dynamic Color.TS palette;
  ≥44pt tap targets via the shared controls.
• i18n (ADR-014): every visible literal resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names;
  interpolated keys use String(format: String(localized:"key"), …) so the key name matches web.

